 "strategy": {
  "summary": "Trade breakouts from the day's normal range, flat by the close. For every time of day the strategy averages how far price has been from that day's open over the last N sessions; times the band multiple, that is the noise band around today's open. At each check time a close above the band goes long and a close below it goes short, at the next bar's open. The position trails out through the band, the session VWAP, or whichever is closer, and is always closed at the session's last close. After Zarattini, Aziz & Barbon (2024).",
  "formula": "band = open \u00b1 multiple \u00d7 average |close \u2212 open| \u00f7 open at this time of day over the last N sessions (\u00d7 today's open)",
  "rules": [
   {
    "label": "Enter",
    "text": "At a check time (every 15, 30 or 60 minutes from the open, and not before the first-entry time), buy when the bar closes above the upper band and sell short when it closes below the lower band. The order fills at the next bar's open. The gap-adjusted anchor starts the upper band from the higher of the open and the prior close, the lower band from the lower."
   },
   {
    "label": "Exit",
    "text": "At a check time, exit when price closes back through the band, through the session VWAP, or through whichever of the two is closer, filled at the next open. Anything still open is closed at the session's last close. No stop loss in this round."
   },
   {
    "label": "Size",
    "text": "Long, short or both; one position at a time, never held overnight; optionally capped at 1 or 2 entries per session; optionally no new entries in the last 60 or 120 minutes; optionally only when the last 30 or 60 minutes moved the same way; optionally skipping breakouts already far beyond the band; optionally only on above-normal volume. As many whole CL contracts as the account covers at full contract value (no leverage), starting from $1,000,000."
   }
  ],
