 "assumptions": [
  "Data: Databento CME continuous front month (CL.v.0), 1-minute bars aggregated to 5 and 15 minutes. Rolls are back-adjusted so the roll gap is not treated as a price move; the band is scaled by the real (unadjusted) open.",
  "Day session only: NYMEX crude day session 09:00-14:30 NY (settlement window) on NYSE trading days. Overnight Globex trading is not used: \"the open\" is the day-session open and the prior close is the previous day-session close. Nothing is held overnight.",
  "Costs: 1 tick slippage per side and $2.50 commission per contract per side, including the session-close exit.",
  "The paper sizes by volatility with up to 4\u00d7 leverage; here each trade uses the whole account in whole contracts with no leverage, the same as the mean-reversion runs.",
  "Session VWAP is built from the 5- or 15-minute bars' typical price and volume, not ticks.",
  "After an exit, a new entry in the same direction waits until price closes back inside the band at a check time; the opposite direction isn't blocked.",
  "With no stop, 5- and 15-minute bars decide at the same check times, and a first-entry time before the first check changes nothing, so the grid contains exact duplicates; they collapse in stage 6.",
  "Sharpe uses daily mark-to-market returns (\u221a252), with idle cash earning 0%. Time in market is the share of bars with an open position.",
  "Holdout (2025 onward) has not been run. It is a one-time final test and needs an explicit go-ahead."
 ],
